Footnote 1: CHE stands for Collisions at High Energies, and it is a Monte-Carlo like code used to access the full kinematics of the final-state particles.

Footnote 2: A method where prediction for W boson production and decay are made based on a calculation for resummation of large logarithmic contributions originating from multiple soft gluon radiation.

